invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: compress_blocks returns without wiping its block_state, so its dead
  frame keeps the last block's message schedule and the state before it.
  Under HMAC-SHA-384 the first block is the key, and the state after it
  stands for the key: whoever reads it computes any MAC under that key.
  Every digest is still right, so no vector sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test
  copies the stack below each kind of call and looks for two 64-bit words
  in a row that the call computed from its input. The file has a body on
  arm64 alone, so the catch is the script, which runs the arm64 binary
  under qemu-aarch64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    run_blocks(&c, h, p, blocks);
    ct_wipe(&c, sizeof c);
--- new
    run_blocks(&c, h, p, blocks);
